# How to cite Solid Memo (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# version and date-released are written by each release, after url
# (docs/releasing.md#what-a-release-does), and are absent until the
# first. Zenodo reads .zenodo.json instead of this file, so the two
# are kept in step by hand (docs/releasing.md#what-a-release-does).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use or refer to Solid Memo, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: Solid Memo
abstract: >-
  Spaced-repetition flashcards that live in your own Solid pod: a static
  web app that schedules cards with SM-2 or FSRS-6 and keeps decks, cards and study
  history in the user's own Solid pod, with a library of ready-made decks,
  courses, and a studio for writing and publishing decks.
authors:
  - given-names: Anton
    family-names: Wiklund
# The concept DOI, which always resolves to the latest version on Zenodo.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23351087
repository-code: https://github.com/solid-memo/website
url: https://solid-memo.com/
version: "5.3.2"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Solid
  - spaced repetition
  - flashcards
  - SM-2
  - FSRS
  - linked data
  - RDF
  - SHACL
  - DCAT
